## Findings
1. blocking — brief:103 The `next` manifest row still has no fail-closed boundary for `source_excludes`: `openStudio` accepts any parseable YAML, while `gather` spreads the raw value, so a scalar can be silently treated as character exclusions and a non-iterable value can throw instead of being rejected by `runNext`; saying that `check` blocks it does not make the named rejector fail closed. — check: packages/cli/src/next.test.ts W-166-b4
2. blocking — brief:13 Sharing the studio repository and using its exclusions does not guarantee that the host can find the recorded commit: `redRepository`/`hashRepo` can accept a detached or other-branch worktree whose HEAD is not reachable from the final opus tip, while the host maps only `rev-list <finalCommit>` and its fallback identifies the parent of the log-introducing commit, not an arbitrary command cwd. State the reachability limit or reject such a cwd. — check: packages/cli/src/red-order.test.ts W-166-b1

## Verdict
The signed revision still has blocking input-boundary and host-reachability gaps.
